# Package Manager

Both projects use **pnpm**. Keep `desktop-vue2/` in its own workspace so Quasar 1 resolves Vue 2. Muya remains in the root workspace.

- Run installation from the repository root with `pnpm install`.
- In `desktop-vue2/`, use `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` and `pnpm add <pkg>` / `pnpm add -D <pkg>`. The app links to Muya with `link:../libs-muya`.
- Use `pnpm --filter libs-muya add <pkg>` / `pnpm --filter libs-muya add -D <pkg>` for the Muya package.
- Run workspace scripts with `pnpm --filter <package-name> <script>`. The root desktop scripts use `pnpm --dir desktop-vue2 run`.
